.u'i

The thing that sparked the initial question was, I was in the car with a guy
from work and we were behind someone who was doing about 30 mph on the one
lane freeway (55 mph) and he finally just screamed "don't you have somewhere
to be".  As in, you're going so slow it seems as though you are out driving
for no real reason because you don't seem to be driving as though you have a
destination in mind.

Only after sending my first email did I realize that usually "don't you have
somewhere to be" usually means "... we need some privacy, don't you have
somewhere else to be (i.e. please leave and go do something else now so that
we'll be alone) or some such.

